pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The same defect one width up. `i128::MIN` does not fit `i64`, so the row is stored as
% `GeneralPBConstraint<i128>` and the wrap simply moves to that type's boundary. This is why the
% fix is checked arithmetic plus escalation and not a wider integer type: widening moves the
% threshold, it does not close the hole.
f 2;
rup 1 x2 >= -170141183460469231731687303715884105728 ;
red 1 ~x1 >= 1 : x1 -> 1 ;
pol 1 4 +;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 5;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
